 GetConnectionOfThread←{
     ⍝ ⍺ ←→ Server
     ⍝ ⍵ ←→ Thread number
     ⍝ ← ←→ The connection served by that thread, or ⍬ when there is none
     ⍝ Every connection is served by a thread of its own (see `WaitForData`), so this answers
     ⍝ "what was this thread working on?" - from an error handler running in that thread, say.
     ⍝ The connection's `Messages` hold what has been received so far, its `LastBlock` the
     ⍝ last block of data exactly as Conga delivered it.
     c←GetConnections ⍺
     0=≢c:⍬
     c←(c.Tid=⍵)/c
     0=≢c:⍬
     ↑c
 }
